The graph shows a $\$24\,000$ asset depreciated by both methods.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=9.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=8.6,ymin=0,ymax=26000,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8},ytick={0,3000,6000,9000,12000,15000,18000,21000,24000},grid=both,samples=60,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years, $n$},ylabel={Value (\$)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:8]{24000 - 3000*x} node[pos=0.15,above right,blue,font=\small]{Straight-line};
\addplot[thick,red,dashed,domain=0:8]{24000*exp(x*ln(0.8))} node[pos=0.625,below left,red,font=\small]{Declining-balance};
